        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0145" n="111" xml:id="pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 73.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[By cable telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1870-09-05"><hi rendition="#small-caps">September</hi> 5,
                            1870</date>. (Received September 5.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish,</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>Chamber met at midnight. Favre proposed dethronement of dynasty. Provisional
                    government to be appointed by Chamber, and that the war shall be continued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WASHBURNE, <hi rendition="#italic">Paris.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
